# Vitest ROM unit tests

Tests live under `src/tests/vitest/` and run from `bin/rom-unittest/`. Folder path selects the fixture — not `describe.skipIf` or env vars inside test files.

| Folder | ROM | Resolver |
|--------|-----|----------|
| `standalone/` | `i2cb`, `i2ce`, `i2ceap6` | `requireConfiglessRomVariants()` |
| `configure/` | INC_CONFIG EAP6 (standalone) or `dist/ap6.rom` (composite) | `requireConfigureFolderVariants()` |
| `fixtures/ap6/` | `dist/ap6.rom` + `ap6-i2c.labels` (embedded I²C) | `requireCompositeRomVariants()` |
| `fixtures/ap6-classic/` | `bin/buildap6/out/ap6-classic.rom` (TreeCopy, no I²C) | `requireClassicCompositeVariants()` |

See `src/tests/vitest/README.md` for Vitest project → npm script mapping.

## Given / When / Then comments (required)

**Every `it(...)` you author or edit gets `// Given —`, `// When —`, `// Then —` comments** — not just sequence/policy tests under `fixtures/`. This is the house style for all ROM tests (`standalone/`, `configure/`, `fixtures/`). When you touch an existing test that lacks them, add them.

Map the three phases to the classic Arrange/Act/Assert (Given/When/Then is the same Four-Phase pattern, per Fowler/North; see martinfowler.com/bliki/GivenWhenThen.html):

- **Given** — preconditions / the state of the world *before* the action: harness construction, `beforeEach` context, RTC/NVRAM/bus mocks, `stubGetrtc`, seeding memory. Describe **state, not actions** ("RTC mock holds BCD 12:34:56"), not a user verb.
- **When** — the **single** action under test: one `invokeCommand` / `invokeBoot` / `invokeService` (or one `run6502`). If a test needs a second When/Then pair (e.g. write-then-read-back), separate the pairs with a fresh `// Given —` (reset captures) + `// When —` + `// Then —`; don't chain unrelated actions under one When.
- **Then** — assertions on **observable** outcomes: MOS output text, returned registers (`A`), memory the command is contracted to write, `mos.unexpected` empty. Prefer outcomes a user/caller can see over internal incidentals.

Style notes:
- One blank `// Given —` line is fine when the precondition is just "harness ready" from `beforeEach`.
- Keep comments declarative (what the ROM does), not a narration of the JS API.
- Do **not** strip these when moving, splitting, or refactoring tests. Do **not** hide star-command steps in helpers when the test should read as a Dave-style sequence — call `invokeCommand` (or explicit NVRAM store setup on classic) in the test body.

Reference style: `standalone/tbrk.test.ts`, `standalone/i2c.test.ts`, `fixtures/ap6/lang-tube-amalgam.test.ts`, `fixtures/ap6-classic/lang-tube-amalgam.test.ts`.

## Fixture-specific behaviour

- **`fixtures/ap6/`** — real `*CONFIGURE` via embedded I²C; amalgam `$8003` for ROM Manager / Plus 1.
- **`fixtures/ap6-classic/`** — no `*CONFIGURE` in ROM; use `writeNVRAMStore` / `writeClassicServ7TubeEnabled` for **NVRAM store** setup; narrative says “NVRAM store”, not “Serv7”.
